# Tests that may skip in `tools/run-tests.sh unit`, each with what it lacks: Class.method<TAB>condition<TAB>reason. A skip not listed
# here fails the unit gate by name; a listed test that runs is named and passes. condition: sem-data (References/sem-data, which
# tools/parity/sem/fetch-data.sh fetches; the nightly sets MACTEM_REQUIRE_SEM_DATA=1 after it, and then no sem-data line allows a skip),
# real-data (the owner's data folder, the suite's References or an opt-in variable: never on a runner), metal, sandbox. Seeded from a
# pull-request run's `unit: SKIPPED` lines (2026-11-10): the Metal tests and the security-scoped bookmark tests run on GitHub's macos-26
# runner, so none of them is listed, and a skip of one fails the gate.
CTFReaderTests.testTheWholeTiFileReadsAsOrix	real-data	opt-in (MACTEM_REAL_DATA=1 or $TMPDIR/macTEM-real-data.flag), then the owner's $MACEM_DATA/sem/Ti_orientations.ctf
